# Line-ending policy.
#
# This working tree lives on a Windows path (C:\code\ai-note-taker) and is
# accessed by BOTH Git for Windows (system autocrlf=true) and Git inside WSL
# (autocrlf unset, i.e. false). Without a fixed policy the two disagree: one
# checks out CRLF, the other flags every line as changed — producing phantom
# whole-file diffs that show in one tool but not the other.
#
# Forcing LF in the index AND the working tree keeps both Gits in agreement.
# `text=auto` lets Git auto-detect binary files and leave them untouched.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Common binary assets — never normalize or diff as text.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif  binary
*.ico  binary
*.svg  text eol=lf
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.pdf  binary

# Append-only tracking tables: resolve concurrent APPENDS automatically.
#
# These three docs are append-heavy and edited by parallel agent sessions. Two sessions
# adding a row each at the end of the same table conflicts every time, purely textually —
# PR #414 re-conflicted three times in one day and never once on code. `merge=union` keeps
# both sides instead of stopping, which is exactly right for an append.
#
# The trade-off, stated plainly: if two branches EDIT THE SAME ROW (both flip a status),
# union keeps BOTH copies rather than picking one, leaving two rows with one id. That is
# why scripts/check-doc-ids.sh runs in the pre-commit hook — it fails on duplicate ids, so
# union's one bad outcome cannot ship silently. Resolve by keeping one row and folding in
# whatever the other added.
#
# NOT applied to docs/roadmap.md: it is prose, so union would interleave sentences into
# nonsense. Its conflicts are fixed differently — by deleting the duplicated bug status
# that lived there (phase-bugs.md is the single source, the roadmap links to it).
docs/phases/phase-bugs.md          merge=union
docs/phases/phase-minor-changes.md merge=union
docs/technical-improvements.md     merge=union
